Package: luxR
Type: Package
Title: Underwater Light Analysis and Visual Ecology
Version: 0.1.1
Date: 2026-11-14
Authors@R: person(given = c("John", "D"),
                   family = "Kirwan",
                   role  = c("aut", "cre"),
                   email = "jkirwan+luxR@pm.me")
Description: Tools for quantifying and modelling underwater light environments.
    Propagates spectral irradiance through the water column via Beer-Lambert
    attenuation, computes photosynthetically active radiation (PAR), and
    converts between energy and photon-flux units. Provides the
    'lux_spectrum' S3 class for unit-safe spectral arithmetic and format
    readers for TriOS RAMSES and Ocean Optics instruments. The optional
    'lightr' package parses further instrument formats into strict native
    records; explicit measurement, scale, calibration, and resampling policies
    govern conversion via read_spectrum(). Spectra convert to and from the
    generic spectral classes of the optional 'photobiology' package, which
    also serves as the reference implementation against which spectral
    integration and photometry are validated. Includes visual ecology
    utilities: visual-pigment templates of Govardovskii et al. (2000)
    <doi:10.1017/S0952523800174036>, photoreceptor quantum catch, colour
    discrimination in just-noticeable differences under the receptor-noise
    model of Vorobyev and Osorio (1998) <doi:10.1098/rspb.1998.0302>, Secchi
    depth, and contrast-threshold distance scenarios, which are explicitly
    not validated.
